              <p>Onyx has confirmed only that the Picco runs on the ESP32 platform and has not named the operating system. In September 2026, Good e-Reader reported that a site which received the device's firmware identified it as a custom fork of CrossPoint — the open-source MIT-licensed e-reader firmware — and specifically not an official CrossPoint release. Treat "ESP32 plus an undisclosed CrossPoint fork" as the most defensible description available.</p>
            </div>
