        <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
          <h3 itemprop="name">Is it legal for a company to fork CrossPoint and ship it closed?</h3>
          <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
            <div itemprop="text">
              <p>Yes. CrossPoint is licensed under the MIT License, which is permissive and explicitly allows commercial use, modification, and redistribution in closed products without any obligation to publish the modifications. The legal question is settled. The practical questions — which version was forked, whether updates will ship, and whether the buyer is told — are where the buyer's risk actually lives.</p>
            </div>
